## Build 4 makes the Chang–Refsdal microlensed likelihood SAMPLEABLE by adding the sampled lens coordinate system, its prior, folding support, and a posterior-boundary refusal net, so a Posterior over CBC+lens parameters runs under cogwheel's standard samplers. The likelihood + engine layers are FROZEN (commit ec8a276, warm lnlike ~9.8 ms/eval); this build only adds the prior/coordinates layer and the minimal serialization/refusal plumbing the sampling layer needs. New module cogwheel/lensing/prior.py holds four lens subpriors (a FixedPrior emitting kappa=0/beta=0/z_lens=0 per the mass-sheet elimination; a log-uniform lens-mass prior; the reduced shear gamma via IdentityTransformMixin; and a mass-conditioned scaled source-position prior with quadrant folding) composed into ONE registered LensedIASPrior whose default_likelihood_class is LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood. A LensedPosterior subclass maps geometry.LensDomainError / operator.CancellationError to lnL=-inf AT THE POSTERIOR BOUNDARY ONLY (engine raise-contract untouched). Pickle/JSON plumbing on the likelihood drops the in-memory _fid_cache for clean deterministic per-worker rebuilds under fork. Distance stays physical (reuse UniformLuminosityVolumePrior; a lens-aware apparent-distance subprior is DEFERRED to Build 5). Injection-recovery validation is a post-build detached driver. ASSUMPTIONS documented: (1) d_L handled via existing UniformLuminosityVolumePrior with mild mu_macro correlation rather than a new d_app subprior (Option A deferred). (2) Only LensedIASPrior is built this cycle; LensedLVCPrior deferred. (3) SPEC needs a new prior-layer row — handled in the post-gate doc-sync phase, not a Coder WP.

### WP1: Lens subpriors module (coordinates + Jacobians + folding)
  What: Create cogwheel/lensing/prior.py with four subprior classes implementing the locked reduced-coordinate parametrization: FixedLensGeometryPrior, UniformLensMassPrior, the reduced-shear gamma subprior, and UniformSourcePositionPrior (with quadrant folding). No combined prior, no registration, no posterior changes here.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/prior.py (new). Mirror the class idioms in cogwheel/gw_prior/extrinsic.py (UniformLuminosityVolumePrior) and cogwheel/gw_prior/mass.py (UniformDetectorFrameMassesPrior); import Prior mixins from cogwheel.prior (FixedPrior, UniformPriorMixin, UnitJacobianMixin, IdentityTransformMixin).
  How: Four classes, each declaring standard_params / range_dic / conditioned_on and the transform/inverse_transform/lnprior/ln_jacobian_determinant contract exactly as the gw_prior templates do.
(a) FixedLensGeometryPrior(FixedPrior): standard_par_dic = {'kappa': 0.0, 'beta': 0.0, 'z_lens': 0.0}. These three are ELIMINATED per Professor constraint 1 (kappa is mass-sheet degenerate) and locked decision (beta circular, z_lens folded into lens mass via w=xi(M_L,z_L)f). range_dic={} inherited from FixedPrior. No transform math.
(b) UniformLensMassPrior(UniformPriorMixin, Prior): sampled param 'ln_m_lens_msun' uniform on [log(10), log(3500)] = [2.302585, 8.160518]; standard_params=['m_lens_msun']; transform: m_lens_msun = exp(ln_m_lens_msun); inverse_transform: ln_m_lens_msun = log(m_lens_msun); ln_jacobian_determinant(ln_m_lens_msun) returns +ln_m_lens_msun? NO — d(m)/d(ln m)=m so ln|J| for sampled->standard density is +ln_m_lens_msun; follow the SIGN CONVENTION already used by UniformDetectorFrameMassesPrior (verify by reading its ln_jacobian_determinant before writing; match it exactly — cogwheel's convention is ln_jacobian_determinant returns the log of d(standard)/d(sampled) mapping used in lnprior_and_transform). Range provenance: upper bound 3500 Msun keeps w=xi*f below the certified w<=500 ceiling across the LIGO band for the crown-config source distance (cite professor/priors_and_coordinates); lower bound 10 Msun keeps diffraction in-band. Add a module constant _LN_M_LENS_RANGE with a comment giving this provenance.
(c) Reduced shear: use IdentityTransformMixin + UniformPriorMixin + UnitJacobianMixin with sampled/standard param name 'gamma' uniform on [0.0, 0.45]. Per Simplifier: do NOT introduce a gamma_prime intermediate — the reduced shear IS the sampled coordinate and is numerically identical to the standard-side gamma the engine consumes, so an identity map with the final name is correct and drops spurious indirection. Upper bound 0.45 leaves positive-parity margin (1-kappa=1 > gamma with headroom; the engine's operator.CancellationError band near gamma_eff~0.5 is excluded from the bulk but can still be hit by curvature — the WP2 refusal net covers the residual).
(d) UniformSourcePositionPrior(UniformPriorMixin, Prior): sampled params ['u1','u2'] on the fixed box [-1,1]x[-1,1]; standard_params=['y1','y2']; conditioned_on=['m_lens_msun']; transform: y1=u1*Y(m), y2=u2*Y(m) where Y(m)=min(307.0/m_lens_msun, 3.0) with module constant _Y_SCALE=307.0 and a comment deriving it (307 = 55/(sqrt(2)*1.2372e-4*1024): keeps w*sqrt(s) below the certified 60 ceiling at the box CORNER, sqrt(2) is the corner factor; cap 3.0 bounds |y| for small lens masses). inverse_transform: u1=y1/Y(m), u2=y2/Y(m). ln_jacobian_determinant = 2*ln(Y(m)) with the SAME sign convention as (b) (d(y1,y2)/d(u1,u2)=Y^2). lnprior=0 (uniform, via UniformPriorMixin). Folding: set folded_reflected_params=['u1','u2'] so cogwheel's standard folding machinery reflects the shear-frame source-angle quadrants (astroid quadrant symmetry, locked decision). Do NOT set any phase fold here (Professor constraint 3: the constant-lens-phase~orbital-phase degeneracy is 22-only and must not be assumed for XPHM).
All four classes: typed params, docstrings citing units (m_lens_msun in solar masses, y dimensionless in shear frame), no I/O, no prints. Verify the exact ln_jacobian_determinant sign/return convention against cogwheel/gw_prior/mass.py and cogwheel/gw_prior/extrinsic.py by reading those bodies FIRST; do not guess the sign.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: cogwheel/lensing/prior.py defines FixedLensGeometryPrior, UniformLensMassPrior, the reduced-shear gamma prior, and UniformSourcePositionPrior; between them the sampled params are {ln_m_lens_msun, gamma, u1, u2} and the emitted standard params are exactly {m_lens_msun, z_lens, y1, y2, gamma, beta, kappa} (the 7 _LENS_PARAMS the likelihood consumes); ln_jacobian_determinant sign/return matches the gw_prior mass/extrinsic convention; UniformSourcePositionPrior.conditioned_on==['m_lens_msun'] and folded_reflected_params==['u1','u2']; no phase-fold param is declared; no engine/likelihood file is modified.
  Max turns: 60

### WP2: Registered LensedIASPrior + LensedPosterior refusal net
  What: Compose the WP1 subpriors with IASPrior's CBC subpriors into ONE registered LensedIASPrior, and add a LensedPosterior subclass that maps engine named refusals to lnL=-inf at the posterior boundary only.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/prior.py (add LensedIASPrior), cogwheel/lensing/posterior.py (new, LensedPosterior) OR append LensedPosterior into an existing lensing module if one already aggregates public API — read cogwheel/lensing/__init__.py first and mirror its export pattern. Registration via RegisteredPriorMixin from cogwheel/gw_prior/combined.py.
  How: 1. LensedIASPrior(RegisteredPriorMixin, CombinedPrior): prior_classes = IASPrior.prior_classes (import IASPrior from cogwheel.gw_prior) + [FixedLensGeometryPrior, UniformLensMassPrior, <reduced-shear gamma prior>, UniformSourcePositionPrior]. Order matters: CombinedPrior requires every conditioned_on param to be produced by an EARLIER subprior — UniformSourcePositionPrior conditioned_on=['m_lens_msun'] so it MUST come after UniformLensMassPrior. Set default_likelihood_class = LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood (import from cogwheel.lensing.likelihood). Distance stays physical: reuse IASPrior's UniformLuminosityVolumePrior unchanged (a lens-aware d_app subprior is DEFERRED to Build 5 — document this in the class docstring). Per Simplifier: build ONLY LensedIASPrior this cycle; do NOT add a LensedLVCPrior. Confirm RegisteredPriorMixin.__init_subclass__ accepts it (no leftover conditioned_on after composition) — the CBC subpriors supply ra/dec/psi/iota/m1/m2 for the distance prior, and m_lens_msun is supplied by UniformLensMassPrior, so all conditioned_on are satisfied.
2. LensedPosterior(Posterior): override lnposterior_pardic_and_metadata to wrap the super() call in try/except (geometry.LensDomainError, operator.CancellationError) and, on catch, return the SAME (-inf, standard_par_dic, None) shape the base returns for np.isneginf(lnprior) (read the base method to match the return tuple exactly). This is the ONLY place refusals are swallowed — Professor constraint 2: the engine/likelihood keep raising named errors; the mapping lives where the sampler meets the posterior. Import the two exception types from cogwheel.lensing.chang_refsdal.geometry and .operator (verify import paths). Per Simplifier: do NOT add an n_refusals counter (process-local, under-counts under fork, misleading — the -inf entries in the sample array are the reliable record). Override from_event/from_reference_waveform_finder ONLY if the base cannot already resolve LensedIASPrior + LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood through the registry; prefer inheriting unchanged.
3. Export LensedIASPrior and LensedPosterior from cogwheel/lensing/__init__.py following the module's existing export convention.
Data-flow: this WP does not change any serialized artifact schema (posterior_config_json gains lens standard params but those already exist in the frozen likelihood's params); no DATA_CONTRACTS change needed (in-memory prior classes only).
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: LensedIASPrior is importable and present in prior_registry, its standard_params set equals LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.params exactly (so Posterior's param-set match passes), prior_classes orders UniformLensMassPrior before UniformSourcePositionPrior, and default_likelihood_class is LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood; LensedPosterior.lnposterior_pardic_and_metadata returns (-inf, dic, None) when the wrapped call raises LensDomainError or CancellationError and is otherwise a pass-through; no n_refusals attribute is added; both classes are exported from cogwheel/lensing/__init__.py; no engine or refusal-threshold code is touched.
  Max turns: 70

### WP3: Fiducial-cache serialization plumbing (fork/pickle safety)
  What: Add __getstate__/__setstate__ to LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood so the in-memory _fid_cache (and only it) is dropped on pickle/fork, giving each sampler worker a clean deterministic per-worker rebuild.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py, LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood only (constructor/serialization plumbing — the ONLY likelihood edit in scope this build).
  How: Read the class first to confirm there is no base __getstate__ (JSONMixin defines get_init_dict for JSON, not pickle state) and that _fid_cache is a plain instance dict initialized in __init__. Add __getstate__ returning self.__dict__ copied with '_fid_cache' removed; add __setstate__ restoring the dict and re-initializing self._fid_cache = {} (empty). Decide _force_direct handling: it is a testing seam / behavioral flag, NOT derived state — PRESERVE it across pickle (keep it in the state dict) so a pickled posterior evaluates identically to its parent; only _fid_cache is dropped. Do not remove or rename _force_direct. Keep get_init_dict unchanged (JSON path already excludes the cache). Add a one-line docstring on __getstate__ explaining WHY the cache is dropped (it is a pure memoization of a deterministic function of the candidate on a fixed lattice, so a forked worker rebuilds identical values on first eval — ~one direct eval per lattice cell per worker, acceptable; determinism preserved). No numerical/threshold code changes.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood defines __getstate__ (excluding _fid_cache, preserving _force_direct and all other state) and __setstate__ (re-initializing _fid_cache to an empty dict); a pickled-then-unpickled instance carries no populated _fid_cache but reproduces the parent's lnlike bit-identically after warm-up; get_init_dict and all refusal thresholds are unchanged.
  Max turns: 40

### Professor Inputs
  - Constraint 1 (build-killer): sample d_app = d_L/sqrt(mu_macro), NEVER kappa — kappa is exactly mass-sheet degenerate and is ELIMINATED (fixed to 0 via FixedPrior), not sampled. beta and z_lens likewise fixed (circular point mass; z_lens folded into w=xi(M_L,z_L)f).
  - Constraint 2 (build-killer): NO unswallowed exceptions under sampler proposals. Bound the prior to strict positive parity AND add a posterior-boundary net mapping geometry.LensDomainError/operator.CancellationError to lnL=-inf; the net lives ONLY where the sampler meets the posterior — the engine/likelihood keep raising named refusals. A net is required because CancellationError can fire in-support (config-curved, not box-bounded).
  - Constraint 3 (build-killer): the constant-lens-phase ~ orbital-phase degeneracy is 22-ONLY; folding must NOT apply any phase-fold for IMRPhenomXPHM higher modes. Build 4 declares no phase-fold param.
  - Reduced coordinates: sample gamma' (reduced shear) and the source position in the SHEAR FRAME; overall amplitude via existing apparent-distance machinery; min-delay convention ties the lens time reference to t_c. ~6 raw lens params reduce to the sampled set {ln lens mass, gamma, shear-frame source position}.
  - Round-2 test tolerances (binding): C1 round-trip atol=rtol=1e-12; C2 Jacobian FD central-difference h_rel=1e-7, |analytic-numeric|<1e-5; C3 domain sweep asserts 1-kappa>|gamma|, w_max<=450, w*sqrt(s)<=58 (margins below certified 500 / 60 ceilings).
  - Round-2 folding tolerance self-correction: brute-force 4-unfold agreement is the TIGHT gate at 1e-6 nats; the RB path must use 0.5 nats because RB approximation error differs per reflected image via fiducial-lattice snapping (an initial 1e-6 for RB was withdrawn as wrong).
  - Mass-sheet check C5 mapping (Professor-supplied): lam=1-kappa, gamma_B=gamma/lam, y_B=y/sqrt(lam), d_L_B=d_L*lam, dt_ms=xi/(4*pi)*(-kappa*s'+ln(lam)), t_B=t_c+dt_ms; brute-force lnL invariance <0.01 nats, RB <0.5 informational.
  - F009 macro limit context: F(w->0)->1/sqrt((1-kappa)**2-gamma**2)=sqrt(mu_macro); this is why sqrt(mu_macro) folds into the apparent distance and kappa is eliminable — confirms the d_app parametrization.
  - Fiducial-cache under fork: per-worker rebuild (~one direct eval per lattice cell per worker) is acceptable and determinism is preserved; drop _fid_cache from pickle state so workers rebuild identical values. No prewarm hook needed for Build 4.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - C1 — Sampled->standard->sampled round-trip identity. Setup: instantiate LensedIASPrior; draw a seeded (np.random.default_rng(0)) sweep of ~2000 points across the full sampled support {ln_m_lens_msun, gamma, u1, u2} plus the CBC sampled params, INCLUDING boundary neighborhoods (endpoints ± 1e-9). Operation: for each point apply transform then inverse_transform. Expected: recovered sampled vector equals the original to atol=1e-12, rtol=1e-12 on every lens coordinate. Diagnostic: scatter of max abs round-trip error vs distance-to-boundary would reveal a boundary-clamping bug in Y(m) or the log map.
  - C2 — Jacobian consistency (finite-difference vs analytic). Setup: seeded ~500 interior points of the lens sampled support. Operation: for UniformLensMassPrior and UniformSourcePositionPrior, compare each class's analytic ln_jacobian_determinant against a central-difference numerical log-determinant of the transform (relative step h_rel=1e-7). Expected: |ln_J_analytic - ln_J_numeric| < 1e-5. Diagnostic: error-vs-m_lens_msun curve would expose a wrong sign or a missing +ln m / +2 ln Y term. NOTE the sign convention must match cogwheel/gw_prior/mass.py (the test derives the numeric determinant from the same transform direction the base lnprior_and_transform uses).
  - C3 — Positive-parity + engine-domain safety over a dense sampled sweep. Setup: 10^4-point seeded grid (Latin-hypercube or rng-uniform) over the ENTIRE sampled support, mapped through transform to standard lens params, using the crown-config source distance/masses for the w scale. Operation: for every mapped point assert (a) 1 - kappa > |gamma| (kappa=0 fixed so gamma<1, but assert the strict inequality on the emitted values), (b) w_max = xi(m_lens,z_lens)*f_max <= 450 (margin below the certified 500 ceiling), (c) w*sqrt(s) <= 58 (margin below the certified 60 product ceiling) with s=|y|^2. Expected: zero violations. Diagnostic: histogram of w_max and of w*sqrt(s) across the sweep — a tail crossing the ceiling would flag a too-wide mass or source-position range.
  - C4a — Folding: F-amplification symmetry under shear-frame source reflection. Setup: seeded set of lens configs; for each, evaluate the engine amplification F(w) at (y1,y2) and at the quadrant reflections (±y1,±y2) directly via ChangRefsdalChannels (NOT via channels-derived fixtures for the expected value — F002 oracle-tautology: build the reflected inputs from raw coordinates only). Expected: |F| is invariant and the delay structure maps consistently under the reflection, to relative < 1e-9, confirming the astroid quadrant symmetry that justifies folded_reflected_params=['u1','u2']. Diagnostic: |F(reflected)-F(original)|/|F| vs quadrant would reveal an asymmetric fold.
  - C4b — Folding: unfold-sum consistency of the folded posterior. Setup: LensedPosterior with LensedIASPrior on the crown-config synthetic event; a small seeded set of folded sampled points. Operation: compare the folded lnposterior (prior.unfold_apply over lnposterior_pardic_and_metadata, logsumexp over the 2^2 reflected u1/u2 images) against an explicit logsumexp of the four individually-unfolded evaluations. Expected: BRUTE-FORCE likelihood path agreement to 1e-6 nats; RELATIVE-BINNING path agreement to 0.5 nats (Professor: RB approximation error differs per reflected image via fiducial-lattice snapping, so the loose bound is correct and the brute path is the tight gate). Diagnostic: per-image lnL table printed alongside the logsumexp would show which reflected image diverges.
  - C4c — Phase-fold is NOT applied for XPHM higher modes. Setup: LensedIASPrior with an IMRPhenomXPHM waveform generator (mode content beyond (2,2)). Operation: inspect the combined prior's folded_shifted_params / folded_reflected_params and confirm no constant-lens-phase~orbital-phase fold is present. Expected: the phase parameter is NOT folded when higher modes are active (Professor constraint 3: the degeneracy is 22-only). Diagnostic: a two-config contrast (22-only vs XPHM) documenting that no phase-fold param is injected in either case for Build 4.
  - C5 — Mass-sheet (d_app) degeneracy: lnL invariance along the eliminated kappa direction. Setup: pick seeded standard lens configs; construct the mass-sheet-transformed twin analytically — lam=1-kappa, gamma_B=gamma/lam, y_B=y/sqrt(lam), d_L_B=d_L*lam, time shift dt_ms = xi/(4*pi)*(-kappa*s' + ln(lam)) applied as t_B = t_c + dt_ms (Professor-supplied mapping). Operation: evaluate the microlensed lnlike at the original and at the transformed twin. Expected: BRUTE-FORCE lnlike agreement < 0.01 nats (the degeneracy is exactly absorbed by sampling d_app rather than kappa); RB path < 0.5 nats (informational). Diagnostic: lnL-difference vs kappa curve should be flat at ~0; a slope would indicate the amplitude/time reference is not correctly tied to the reduced coordinates.
  - C6 — Refusal net returns exactly -inf, never an exception, and the raw path still raises. Setup: engineer seeded proposals whose curvature drives gamma_eff into the operator.CancellationError band (gamma sampled near 0.48–0.499 combined with a source position that pushes w*sqrt(s) toward the product ceiling) so the engine issues a NAMED refusal in-support. Operation: (a) evaluate LensedPosterior.lnposterior_pardic_and_metadata on these configs; (b) evaluate the SAME configs through the raw LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike (or an UnboundedLensedPosterior test double that does NOT catch). Expected: (a) returns exactly -inf (np.isneginf True) with the correct return-tuple shape and NO exception escaping; (b) raises geometry.LensDomainError or operator.CancellationError. This proves the net lives only at the posterior boundary and the engine contract is preserved. Diagnostic: assert on exception type in (b) and on np.isneginf in (a). MUTATION CHECK: temporarily narrowing the except clause to not catch CancellationError must turn (a) RED.
  - C7 — End-to-end sampling smoke. Setup: build LensedPosterior on the crown-config synthetic event via the registry (prior_class=LensedIASPrior). Operation: draw ~500 seeded prior samples (rng fixed) and evaluate lnposterior on each. Expected: zero exceptions; every result is finite OR exactly -inf; at least ~90% are finite (bounded support keeps most proposals in the certified domain); the maximum lnposterior over the draws is within ~50 nats of the value at the injected parameters (sanity that the peak is near truth). Diagnostic: histogram of lnposterior with the injected-parameter value marked; a peak far from the injection or a large -inf fraction flags a coordinate/range bug.

